    "body": "I've create such test and it fails so I think no. Should it also handle that case? I don't quite understand `map_meta` for now\r\n```rust\r\n    #[test]\r\n    fn test_empty_meta_variable() {\r\n        const FORMAT_STR: &str = \"$all\";\r\n        const FORMAT_STR__ALL: &str = \"$a$b\";\r\n\r\n        let formatter = StringFormatter::new(FORMAT_STR)\r\n            .unwrap()\r\n            .map_meta(|var, _| match var {\r\n                \"all\" => Some(FORMAT_STR__ALL),\r\n                _ => None,\r\n            })\r\n            .map(|var| match var {\r\n                \"a\" => Some(Ok(\"\")),\r\n                \"b\" => Some(Ok(\"\")),\r\n                _ => None,\r\n            });\r\n        let result = formatter.parse(None).unwrap();\r\n        assert_eq!(result.len(), 0);\r\n    }\r\n```",
